;; LOCALLY-MINTED declarations: shapes this generator declares itself, which no
;; descriptor database carries.
;;
;; A MINT DECLARES NO FIELD NUMBER, AND THE SCHEMA HAS NO KEY FOR ONE. That is
;; what leaves `numbering-registry.edn` as the only possible source of one — the
;; generator refuses to run against an unpinned field rather than inventing one,
;; so a number here cannot move because a policy changed.
;;
;; EACH DECLARATION IS TAGGED `:kind`, and the two kinds are numbered by
;; different mechanisms for a reason stated in `protocol-gen.numbering`: a
;; MESSAGE's fields take the registry's numbers, while an ENUM's members carry
;; their own, because the registry's value schema excludes 0 and proto3 requires
;; an enum member numbered 0.
;;
;; A MINTED ONEOF NAMES ITS MEMBERS BY FIELD NAME, where a database oneof names
;; them by number. A mint has no numbers to name them with; the stamping pass
;; resolves each name against this message's own fields, so a member naming
;; something not below is REFUSED rather than dropped.
;;
;; `pgfix.Notice` is deliberately awkward in three ways at once, because a
;; fixture that is tidy cannot tell a correct generator from a lucky one:
;;
;;   * its registry pins are non-contiguous AND out of declaration order, so a
;;     generator numbering by position emits 1/2/3 and is caught;
;;   * its oneof's members are pinned so that NUMBER order and DECLARATION order
;;     disagree, so an emitter listing members as declared is caught too;
;;   * it carries a free field beside the oneof, and refers to a minted enum
;;     that exists in no database — the reference resolves only if enum
;;     resolution consults the universe rather than the database.
{"pgfix.Heartbeat"
 {:kind :message
  :name "Heartbeat"
  :fields [{:name "seq" :type :uint32 :constraints {:gte 1}}
           {:name "sent_at_ns" :type :uint64}]}

 "pgfix.Level"
 {:kind :enum
  :name "Level"
  :values [{:number 0 :name "LEVEL_UNSPECIFIED"}
           {:number 3 :name "LEVEL_INFO"}
           {:number 12 :name "LEVEL_ALERT"}]}

 "pgfix.Notice"
 {:kind :message
  :name "Notice"
  :fields [{:name "level" :type :enum :type-ref "pgfix.Level"
            :constraints {:defined-only true}}
           {:name "text" :type :string :constraints {:min-len 1}}
           {:name "code" :type :uint32}]
  :oneofs [{:name "detail" :required true :fields ["text" "code"]}]}}
